			<div class="content" id="post-content-2491161">
									

<p>This is amusing.</p>
<p>There's a couple of grammatical errors in the piece (an &quot;at at&quot; at one point, for example) but nothing that can't be overcome. I have to admit, the greatest problem I have with it would be the Foundation's decision to keep a sheet of peep-chirp in the file, when it would make more sense to transcribe the conversation later (proven possible by &quot;splashy time&quot;, &quot;Daisy&quot;, and &quot;Tissle&quot;), outside the area of effect. That said, I'm still upvoting because it's cute and funny, and I'm still thinking about how you'd have problems understanding their capabilities - or the conversations you could have with others near the birds that couldn't be recorded.</p>

							</div>

								
					
