			<div class="content" id="post-content-2491469">
									

<p>This was entertaining enough for me to upvote. A lighthearted anomaly that doesn't crush my soul is a very needed breath of fresh air every now and then.</p>
<p>I will say that you do a lot of blackboxing here that is not really necessary. This doesn't seem like the kind of SCP object that would warrant such high levels of censorship. You'd be better off just including the names. Also, blackboxing in the containment procedures is not something you should do if it can be helped, since that is the most crucial information from an in-universe standpoint, since thats how the object remains secured, contained, and protected.</p>
<p>But hey, thats just my opinion.</p>

